//@version=6
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// MummyTKT's Entry Confirmations v9 — TradingView Edition (2026-11-25: OCTGD 2 = first two in a row; OCTGD 3; void rule on the server)
//
// Companion indicator to MummyTKT's Bias Pointer.
// MARKS: each timeframe's confirmations show on that timeframe's own chart: H1 ones on
// an H1 chart, H2 on H2, M15 on M15, M5 on M5 (put the chart on the one you study).
// CHART: each alert carries that timeframe's last 30 candles, so the Telegram message comes with a chart picture.
// LIMIT (2026-11-16): after the candles, "|<buy breaker>|<sell breaker>" of a Sweep and Break (a limit entry's price).
// MEMORY: the H1 / H2 / M15 / M5 reads only run on a 5-minute (or smaller) chart, where alerts are sent
// (on bigger charts they read the monthly candles); the alert's candle text is only built for the last 3 days.
// ALERTS: put it on a 5-minute chart (the smallest timeframe it reads) for each
// instrument and create ONE alert:
//   condition = "Any alert() function call"
//   webhook   = https://forex-radar.fly.dev/api/tv-webhook
// It reads H1, H2, M15 and M5 from that one chart (each on its own candles) and sends
// every confirmation with its timeframe. The dashboard's entry alerts decide which ones
// you hear about: each level (your POI) watches the confirmations you tick, within your
// tolerance.
//
// Confirmations (buys; sells are the mirror). Each is judged when its candle closes.
//   PCL — H1 (the same as the H1 Sweep)
//       C1 is bearish. C2 is bullish: its wick goes BELOW C1's low and its body closes
//       back ABOVE that low.
//   OCTGD 1 (Open Close That Got Disrespected) — H1 / M15
//       The last two bearish candles (C1, C2) form a bearish OC; its level is where C1
//       closes and C2 opens. C2 is the candle that touched the POI (or both formed
//       inside it). Then, within a few candles, a bullish candle closes ABOVE that level.
//       A newer bearish OC replaces the older one.
//   OCTGD 2 — H1 / M15 (owner rule 2026-11-25)
//       After a NEW touch of your level, the FIRST two bullish candles in a row (bearish candles
//       before them don't matter) = OCTGD 2; their OC (C1's close) is the entry, the pair's wick
//       the SL. Only the level's first touch (later: a re-entry after an SL). The script sends every
//       pair that starts a bullish run; the server judges it against each of your levels from the
//       candles in the alert (the chart has no marks for it).
//   VOID (server): after the touch, a candle that CLOSES below the low of the first bullish candle
//       voids an OCTGD 1 / OCTGD 3 still forming (a wick below doesn't); other confirmations count.
//   OCTGD 3 — H1 / M15 (owner rule 2026-11-25)
//       After price has touched your level, the LAST bearish candle; a bullish candle then closes
//       above that bearish candle's OPEN = OCTGD 3. Entry = a limit at that open, SL = the wick
//       since the touch. The script sends every bullish close above the last bearish open; the
//       server checks your level was touched before that bearish candle (no chart marks).
//   Sweep and Break — M15 / M5
//       A fractal low forms (a low below the 2 candles on each side). A candle's wick
//       goes below it and closes back above (the sweep). Then, before a close below
//       the sweep wick, a candle body closes above the last fractal high before the
//       sweep (the last lower high): the break.
//   CISD (Change in State of Delivery) — H1 / M15 / M5
//       A series of 2 or more bearish candles IN A ROW delivers price down (one bearish
//       candle alone is not a series, user 2026-11-19). The CISD line is the OPEN of the
//       first candle of the series that made the lowest low (a smaller pullback series that
//       doesn't go lower doesn't replace it). A bullish candle's body closing ABOVE that
//       line is the CISD. Judged on opens and closes, not wicks.
//   Engulfing — H1 / H2 (one confirmation, whichever kind shows)
//       C1 is bearish. C2 is bullish, opens at or below C1's close and closes above C1's
//       open (its body covers C1's body). When it also closes above C1's HIGH, its body
//       covers the wick too, and the alert says so.
// Each webhook carries "touch_price" (the wick that reached your level); the server
// checks your tolerance against it.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

indicator("MummyTKT Entry Confirmations", overlay = true, max_bars_back = 500, max_labels_count = 200)

string wh_secret = input.string("", "Webhook Secret", tooltip = "Paste your TV_WEBHOOK_SECRET value here")
bool   use_h1  = input.bool(true, "H1 (PCL, OCTGD 1-3, CISD, Engulfing)", group = "Timeframes read from this chart", inline = "t1")
bool   use_h2  = input.bool(true, "H2 (Engulfing)", group = "Timeframes read from this chart", inline = "t1")
bool   use_m15 = input.bool(true, "M15 (OCTGD 1-3, Sweep and Break, CISD)", group = "Timeframes read from this chart", inline = "t2")
bool   use_m5  = input.bool(true, "M5 (Sweep and Break, CISD)", group = "Timeframes read from this chart", inline = "t2")
int    fr_n    = input.int(2, "Sweep and Break: fractal candles each side", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = "Sweep and Break")
int    sb_win  = input.int(20, "Candles allowed from the sweep to the break", minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = "Sweep and Break")
int    oc_win  = input.int(10, "OCTGD: candles allowed from C2 to the close through the level", minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = "OCTGD")
int    ci_win  = input.int(20, "CISD: candles allowed from the low to the close through the line", minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = "CISD")
bool   show_mk = input.bool(true, "Show the confirmations on the chart", group = "Markers")
bool   show_nt = input.bool(false, "Show the note on charts with no marks (4h, Daily, ...)", group = "Markers")
color  bull_col = input.color(color.new(color.green, 10), "Bullish", group = "Markers", inline = "mc")
color  bear_col = input.color(color.new(color.red, 10), "Bearish", group = "Markers", inline = "mc")

// ── The confirmations on one timeframe's candles ─────────────────────────────
// Returns this timeframe's last COMPLETED candle (through [1] + lookahead_on below)
f_forms(simple int n, simple int win, simple int ow, simple int cw) =>
    bool pbull = close[1] > open[1]
    bool pbear = close[1] < open[1]
    bool cbull = close > open
    bool cbear = close < open
    // PCL (= the Sweep): wick past C1's low (high), body closes back above (below) it
    bool b_pcl = pbear and cbull and low < low[1] and close > low[1]
    bool s_pcl = pbull and cbear and high > high[1] and close < high[1]
    // Engulfing: C2's body covers C1's body; "wick" when it also closes beyond C1's high (low)
    bool b_en  = pbear and cbull and open <= close[1] and close > open[1]
    bool s_en  = pbull and cbear and open >= close[1] and close < open[1]
    bool b_enw = b_en and close > high[1]
    bool s_enw = s_en and close < low[1]
    // OCTGD: the latest OC waits for a close through its level the other way
    var float boc_lv = na    // bearish OC (for a buy): C1 close = C2 open
    var float boc_tp = na    // its wick at the POI: the lower low of C1 / C2
    var int   boc_b  = na
    var float soc_lv = na    // bullish OC (for a sell)
    var float soc_tp = na
    var int   soc_b  = na
    bool  b_oc = false
    bool  s_oc = false
    float b_oclv = na
    float b_octp = na
    float s_oclv = na
    float s_octp = na
    // checked before this candle can start a new OC (a candle is never both)
    if not na(boc_lv)
        if bar_index - boc_b > ow
            boc_lv := na
        else if cbull and close > boc_lv
            b_oc   := true
            b_oclv := boc_lv
            b_octp := boc_tp
            boc_lv := na
    if not na(soc_lv)
        if bar_index - soc_b > ow
            soc_lv := na
        else if cbear and close < soc_lv
            s_oc   := true
            s_oclv := soc_lv
            s_octp := soc_tp
            soc_lv := na
    if pbear and cbear
        boc_lv := close[1]
        boc_tp := math.min(low, low[1])
        boc_b  := bar_index
    if pbull and cbull
        soc_lv := close[1]
        soc_tp := math.max(high, high[1])
        soc_b  := bar_index
    // CISD: the run of candles that delivered price to its low (high), and the open of its first candle
    var float dn_open = na    // the current bearish run: open of its first candle
    var int   dn_n    = 0     // candles in the current bearish run (a CISD series needs 2+ in a row, user 2026-11-19)
    var float dn_low  = na    // ... and its lowest low
    var float bci_ln  = na    // buy CISD line
    var float bci_lo  = na    // lowest low since that run began (the wick at your level)
    var int   bci_b   = na    // candle that made that low
    var float up_open = na
    var int   up_n    = 0
    var float up_high = na
    var float sci_ln  = na    // sell CISD line
    var float sci_hi  = na
    var int   sci_b   = na
    bool  b_ci = false
    bool  s_ci = false
    float b_cilv = na
    float b_citp = na
    float s_cilv = na
    float s_citp = na
    // checked before this candle can change the run
    if not na(bci_ln)
        if low < bci_lo
            bci_lo := low
            bci_b  := bar_index
        if bar_index - bci_b > cw
            bci_ln := na
        else if cbull and close > bci_ln
            b_ci   := true
            b_cilv := bci_ln
            b_citp := bci_lo
            bci_ln := na
    if not na(sci_ln)
        if high > sci_hi
            sci_hi := high
            sci_b  := bar_index
        if bar_index - sci_b > cw
            sci_ln := na
        else if cbear and close < sci_ln
            s_ci   := true
            s_cilv := sci_ln
            s_citp := sci_hi
            sci_ln := na
    if cbear
        if not pbear
            dn_open := open
            dn_low  := low
            dn_n    := 1
        else
            dn_low  := math.min(dn_low, low)
            dn_n    += 1
        // the run that delivered price lowest is the one; a pullback run that doesn't go lower doesn't replace it
        if not b_ci and dn_n >= 2 and (na(bci_ln) or dn_low <= bci_lo)
            bci_ln := dn_open
            bci_lo := dn_low
            bci_b  := bar_index
    if cbull
        if not pbull
            up_open := open
            up_high := high
            up_n    := 1
        else
            up_high := math.max(up_high, high)
            up_n    += 1
        if not s_ci and up_n >= 2 and (na(sci_ln) or up_high >= sci_hi)
            sci_ln := up_open
            sci_hi := up_high
            sci_b  := bar_index
    // Sweep and Break
    var float fl  = na    // latest fractal low not yet swept
    var float fh  = na    // latest fractal high not yet swept
    var float lfh = na    // latest fractal high (the last lower high for a buy)
    var float lfl = na    // latest fractal low (the last higher low for a sell)
    float ph = ta.pivothigh(high, n, n)
    float pl = ta.pivotlow(low, n, n)
    if not na(ph)
        fh  := ph
        lfh := ph
    if not na(pl)
        fl  := pl
        lfl := pl
    var bool  bs_on = false
    var float bs_lo = na
    var float bs_lv = na
    var float bs_br = na
    var int   bs_b  = na
    var bool  ss_on = false
    var float ss_hi = na
    var float ss_lv = na
    var float ss_br = na
    var int   ss_b  = na
    if not na(fl) and low < fl and close > fl
        bs_on := not na(lfh) and lfh > close
        bs_lo := low
        bs_lv := fl
        bs_br := lfh
        bs_b  := bar_index
        fl := na
    if not na(fh) and high > fh and close < fh
        ss_on := not na(lfl) and lfl < close
        ss_hi := high
        ss_lv := fh
        ss_br := lfl
        ss_b  := bar_index
        fh := na
    bool  b_sb = false
    bool  s_sb = false
    float b_lv = na
    float b_tp = na
    float s_lv = na
    float s_tp = na
    float b_br = na     // the lower high it broke (a buy's limit)
    float s_br = na     // the higher low it broke (a sell's limit)
    if bs_on
        if close < bs_lo or bar_index - bs_b > win
            bs_on := false
        else if close > bs_br
            b_sb := true
            b_lv := bs_lv
            b_tp := bs_lo
            b_br := bs_br
            bs_on := false
    if ss_on
        if close > ss_hi or bar_index - ss_b > win
            ss_on := false
        else if close < ss_br
            s_sb := true
            s_lv := ss_lv
            s_tp := ss_hi
            s_br := ss_br
            ss_on := false
    // OCTGD 2 candidates (2026-11-25): two candles in a row the trade's way, right after a new low (buy) / high
    // (sell): C1 made it, or C0 made it against the trade. The server checks them against each level.
    bool b_o2 = pbull and cbull and not (close[2] > open[2])     // the first two of a bullish run
    bool s_o2 = pbear and cbear and not (close[2] < open[2])     // the first two of a bearish run
    // OCTGD 3 candidates (2026-11-25): a bullish (bearish) close above (below) the open of the last bearish
    // (bullish) candle, within the OCTGD window; the server checks the level was touched before that candle
    var float lb_o = na
    var int   lb_b = na
    var float ls_o = na
    var int   ls_b = na
    bool b_o3 = cbull and not na(lb_o) and bar_index - lb_b <= ow and close > lb_o
    bool s_o3 = cbear and not na(ls_o) and bar_index - ls_b <= ow and close < ls_o
    if b_o3
        lb_o := na
    if s_o3
        ls_o := na
    if cbear
        lb_o := open
        lb_b := bar_index
    if cbull
        ls_o := open
        ls_b := bar_index
    // The last 30 candles (oldest first) for the alert's chart picture: "minutes,o,h,l,c;..."
    string cs = ""
    // only the last 3 days build it (alerts are live): old candles keep an empty text, which saves memory
    if (b_pcl or s_pcl or b_en or s_en or b_oc or s_oc or b_sb or s_sb or b_ci or s_ci or b_o2 or s_o2 or b_o3 or s_o3) and time > timenow - 3 * 86400000
        for i = 29 to 0
            if not na(close[i]) and not na(time[i])
                cs += (cs == "" ? "" : ";") + str.tostring(math.floor(time[i] / 60000)) + "," + str.tostring(open[i], format.mintick) + ","
                     + str.tostring(high[i], format.mintick) + "," + str.tostring(low[i], format.mintick) + "," + str.tostring(close[i], format.mintick)
        if b_sb or s_sb      // the breaker rides in the same text (no extra values: the script is near its memory limit)
            cs += "|" + (na(b_br) ? "" : str.tostring(b_br)) + "|" + (na(s_br) ? "" : str.tostring(s_br))
        // the OCTGD 2 flags ride at the end of the same text (no extra values: memory)
        if b_o2
            cs += "|o2b"
        if s_o2
            cs += "|o2s"
        if b_o3
            cs += "|o3b"
        if s_o3
            cs += "|o3s"
    [b_pcl, s_pcl, b_en, s_en, b_enw, s_enw, b_oc, s_oc, b_sb, s_sb, close, low, high, low[1], high[1], open[1],
     math.min(low, low[1]), math.max(high, high[1]), b_oclv, b_octp, s_oclv, s_octp, b_lv, b_tp, s_lv, s_tp, time,
     b_ci, s_ci, b_cilv, b_citp, s_cilv, s_citp, cs]

f_prev(simple int n, simple int win, simple int ow, simple int cw) =>
    [a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6, a7, a8, a9, a10, a11, a12, a13, a14, a15, a16, a17, a18, a19, a20, a21, a22, a23, a24, a25, a26, a27, a28, a29, a30, a31, a32, a33, a34] = f_forms(n, win, ow, cw)
    [a1[1], a2[1], a3[1], a4[1], a5[1], a6[1], a7[1], a8[1], a9[1], a10[1], a11[1], a12[1], a13[1], a14[1], a15[1], a16[1], a17[1], a18[1],
     a19[1], a20[1], a21[1], a22[1], a23[1], a24[1], a25[1], a26[1], a27[1], a28[1], a29[1], a30[1], a31[1], a32[1], a33[1], a34[1]]

// Alerts are sent from a 5-minute (or smaller) chart only. On a bigger chart these four reads are not used (its
// marks come from the chart's own candles), so they read the monthly candles: a few hundred bars, almost no memory.
bool   sec_ok = timeframe.in_seconds() <= 300
string tf_h1  = sec_ok ? "60" : "1M"
string tf_h2  = sec_ok ? "120" : "1M"
string tf_m15 = sec_ok ? "15" : "1M"
string tf_m5  = sec_ok ? "5" : "1M"
[h1_bpcl, h1_spcl, h1_ben, h1_sen, h1_benw, h1_senw, h1_boc, h1_soc, h1_bsb, h1_ssb, h1_c, h1_l, h1_h, h1_pl, h1_ph, h1_po, h1_lo2, h1_hi2, h1_boclv, h1_boctp, h1_soclv, h1_soctp, h1_blv, h1_btp, h1_slv, h1_stp, h1_t, h1_bci, h1_sci, h1_bcilv, h1_bcitp, h1_scilv, h1_scitp, h1_cs] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf_h1, f_prev(fr_n, sb_win, oc_win, ci_win), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[h2_bpcl, h2_spcl, h2_ben, h2_sen, h2_benw, h2_senw, h2_boc, h2_soc, h2_bsb, h2_ssb, h2_c, h2_l, h2_h, h2_pl, h2_ph, h2_po, h2_lo2, h2_hi2, h2_boclv, h2_boctp, h2_soclv, h2_soctp, h2_blv, h2_btp, h2_slv, h2_stp, h2_t, h2_bci, h2_sci, h2_bcilv, h2_bcitp, h2_scilv, h2_scitp, h2_cs] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf_h2, f_prev(fr_n, sb_win, oc_win, ci_win), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[m15_bpcl, m15_spcl, m15_ben, m15_sen, m15_benw, m15_senw, m15_boc, m15_soc, m15_bsb, m15_ssb, m15_c, m15_l, m15_h, m15_pl, m15_ph, m15_po, m15_lo2, m15_hi2, m15_boclv, m15_boctp, m15_soclv, m15_soctp, m15_blv, m15_btp, m15_slv, m15_stp, m15_t, m15_bci, m15_sci, m15_bcilv, m15_bcitp, m15_scilv, m15_scitp, m15_cs] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf_m15, f_prev(fr_n, sb_win, oc_win, ci_win), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[r5_bpcl, r5_spcl, r5_ben, r5_sen, r5_benw, r5_senw, r5_boc, r5_soc, r5_bsb, r5_ssb, r5_c, r5_l, r5_h, r5_pl, r5_ph, r5_po, r5_lo2, r5_hi2, r5_boclv, r5_boctp, r5_soclv, r5_soctp, r5_blv, r5_btp, r5_slv, r5_stp, r5_t, r5_bci, r5_sci, r5_bcilv, r5_bcitp, r5_scilv, r5_scitp, r5_cs] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf_m5, f_prev(fr_n, sb_win, oc_win, ci_win), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
// The chart's own candles: its marks (H1 / H2 / M15 / M5 chart), and on a 5-minute chart the M5 alerts (no one-candle delay)
[d5_bpcl, d5_spcl, d5_ben, d5_sen, d5_benw, d5_senw, d5_boc, d5_soc, d5_bsb, d5_ssb, d5_c, d5_l, d5_h, d5_pl, d5_ph, d5_po, d5_lo2, d5_hi2, d5_boclv, d5_boctp, d5_soclv, d5_soctp, d5_blv, d5_btp, d5_slv, d5_stp, d5_t, d5_bci, d5_sci, d5_bcilv, d5_bcitp, d5_scilv, d5_scitp, d5_cs] = f_forms(fr_n, sb_win, oc_win, ci_win)
bool m5_own = timeframe.in_seconds() == 300

bool chart_ok = timeframe.in_seconds() <= 300

f_send(string pat, string dir, string tf, float price, float swept, float touch, string kind, string cs) =>
    alert('{"secret":"' + wh_secret + '","type":"ENTRY_CONFIRMATION","instrument":"' + syminfo.ticker + '","pattern":"' + pat
         + '","direction":"' + dir + '","timeframe":"' + tf + '","price":' + str.tostring(price) + ',"swept_level":' + str.tostring(swept)
         + ',"touch_price":' + str.tostring(touch) + (kind != "" ? ',"kind":"' + kind + '"' : '') + (cs != "" ? ',"candles":"' + cs + '"' : '') + '}', alert.freq_once_per_bar)

f_mark(bool mk, string txt, bool bull, string tip) =>
    if show_mk and mk
        label.new(bar_index, bull ? low : high, txt, yloc = bull ? yloc.belowbar : yloc.abovebar,
             style = bull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = bull ? bull_col : bear_col,
             textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, tooltip = tip)

// One timeframe: once its candle has closed, mark (mk) and/or send (snd) what formed.
// pcl / oc / en / sb / ci say which confirmations this timeframe watches.
f_tf(bool on, bool mk, bool snd, bool conf, string tf, string nm, int t, bool pcl, bool oc, bool en, bool sb, bool ci, bool o2,
     bool bpcl, bool spcl, bool ben, bool sen, bool benw, bool senw, bool boc, bool soc, bool bsb, bool ssb,
     float c, float l, float h, float pl, float ph, float po, float lo2, float hi2,
     float boclv, float boctp, float soclv, float soctp, float blv, float btp, float slv, float stp,
     bool bci, bool sci, float bcilv, float bcitp, float scilv, float scitp, string cs) =>
    bool newc = not na(t) and t != t[1]
    if on and newc and conf
        bool rt = barstate.isrealtime
        if pcl and bpcl
            f_mark(mk, nm + " PCL", true, nm + " bullish PCL: wick below the bearish candle's low, closed back above it")
            if rt and snd
                f_send("pcl", "bullish", tf, c, pl, l, "", cs)
        if pcl and spcl
            f_mark(mk, nm + " PCL", false, nm + " bearish PCL: wick above the bullish candle's high, closed back below it")
            if rt and snd
                f_send("pcl", "bearish", tf, c, ph, h, "", cs)
        if oc and boc
            f_mark(mk, nm + " OCTGD 1", true, nm + " bullish OCTGD 1: closed above the bearish OC level " + str.tostring(boclv, format.mintick))
            if rt and snd
                f_send("octgd", "bullish", tf, c, boclv, boctp, "", cs)
        if oc and soc
            f_mark(mk, nm + " OCTGD 1", false, nm + " bearish OCTGD 1: closed below the bullish OC level " + str.tostring(soclv, format.mintick))
            if rt and snd
                f_send("octgd", "bearish", tf, c, soclv, soctp, "", cs)
        // OCTGD 2: sent for the server to judge against your level (no mark: the chart doesn't know your level)
        if o2 and rt and snd and str.contains(cs, "|o2b")
            f_send("octgd2", "bullish", tf, c, c, lo2, "", cs)
        if o2 and rt and snd and str.contains(cs, "|o2s")
            f_send("octgd2", "bearish", tf, c, c, hi2, "", cs)
        // OCTGD 3 rides the same switch (H1 / M15): the server checks your level was touched first
        if o2 and rt and snd and str.contains(cs, "|o3b")
            f_send("octgd3", "bullish", tf, c, c, lo2, "", cs)
        if o2 and rt and snd and str.contains(cs, "|o3s")
            f_send("octgd3", "bearish", tf, c, c, hi2, "", cs)
        if en and ben
            f_mark(mk, nm + " Engulf", true, nm + " bullish Engulfing: " + (benw ? "body closed above the bearish candle's high (wick)" : "body covered the bearish candle's body"))
            if rt and snd
                f_send("engulfing", "bullish", tf, c, benw ? ph : po, lo2, benw ? "wick" : "body", cs)
        if en and sen
            f_mark(mk, nm + " Engulf", false, nm + " bearish Engulfing: " + (senw ? "body closed below the bullish candle's low (wick)" : "body covered the bullish candle's body"))
            if rt and snd
                f_send("engulfing", "bearish", tf, c, senw ? pl : po, hi2, senw ? "wick" : "body", cs)
        if ci and bci
            f_mark(mk, nm + " CISD", true, nm + " bullish CISD: closed above the open of the bearish run, " + str.tostring(bcilv, format.mintick))
            if rt and snd
                f_send("cisd", "bullish", tf, c, bcilv, bcitp, "", cs)
        if ci and sci
            f_mark(mk, nm + " CISD", false, nm + " bearish CISD: closed below the open of the bullish run, " + str.tostring(scilv, format.mintick))
            if rt and snd
                f_send("cisd", "bearish", tf, c, scilv, scitp, "", cs)
        if sb and bsb
            f_mark(mk, nm + " S&B", true, nm + " bullish Sweep and Break: low swept at " + str.tostring(btp, format.mintick) + ", lower high broken")
            if rt and snd
                f_send("sweep_break", "bullish", tf, c, blv, btp, "", cs)
        if sb and ssb
            f_mark(mk, nm + " S&B", false, nm + " bearish Sweep and Break: high swept at " + str.tostring(stp, format.mintick) + ", higher low broken")
            if rt and snd
                f_send("sweep_break", "bearish", tf, c, slv, stp, "", cs)

// ALERTS from a 5-minute (or smaller) chart: H1, H2 and M15 read through their own candles
// (sent only, no marks: the marks belong on each timeframe's own chart)
f_tf(use_h1 and chart_ok, false, true, true, "60", "H1", h1_t, true, true, true, false, true, true,
     h1_bpcl, h1_spcl, h1_ben, h1_sen, h1_benw, h1_senw, h1_boc, h1_soc, h1_bsb, h1_ssb,
     h1_c, h1_l, h1_h, h1_pl, h1_ph, h1_po, h1_lo2, h1_hi2, h1_boclv, h1_boctp, h1_soclv, h1_soctp, h1_blv, h1_btp, h1_slv, h1_stp,
     h1_bci, h1_sci, h1_bcilv, h1_bcitp, h1_scilv, h1_scitp, h1_cs)
f_tf(use_h2 and chart_ok, false, true, true, "120", "H2", h2_t, false, false, true, false, false, false,
     h2_bpcl, h2_spcl, h2_ben, h2_sen, h2_benw, h2_senw, h2_boc, h2_soc, h2_bsb, h2_ssb,
     h2_c, h2_l, h2_h, h2_pl, h2_ph, h2_po, h2_lo2, h2_hi2, h2_boclv, h2_boctp, h2_soclv, h2_soctp, h2_blv, h2_btp, h2_slv, h2_stp,
     h2_bci, h2_sci, h2_bcilv, h2_bcitp, h2_scilv, h2_scitp, h2_cs)
f_tf(use_m15 and chart_ok, false, true, true, "15", "M15", m15_t, false, true, false, true, true, true,
     m15_bpcl, m15_spcl, m15_ben, m15_sen, m15_benw, m15_senw, m15_boc, m15_soc, m15_bsb, m15_ssb,
     m15_c, m15_l, m15_h, m15_pl, m15_ph, m15_po, m15_lo2, m15_hi2, m15_boclv, m15_boctp, m15_soclv, m15_soctp, m15_blv, m15_btp, m15_slv, m15_stp,
     m15_bci, m15_sci, m15_bcilv, m15_bcitp, m15_scilv, m15_scitp, m15_cs)
// M5 on a chart below 5 minutes (on a 5-minute chart the call below sends it from the chart's own candles)
f_tf(use_m5 and chart_ok and not m5_own, false, true, true, "5", "M5", r5_t, false, false, false, true, true, false,
     false, false, false, false, false, false, false, false, r5_bsb, r5_ssb,
     r5_c, na, na, na, na, na, na, na, na, na, na, na, r5_blv, r5_btp, r5_slv, r5_stp,
     r5_bci, r5_sci, r5_bcilv, r5_bcitp, r5_scilv, r5_scitp, r5_cs)

// MARKS on the chart's own timeframe: H1 chart = H1 confirmations, H2 = H2, M15 = M15, M5 = M5
string own_tf  = timeframe.period
bool   own_h1  = own_tf == "60"
bool   own_h2  = own_tf == "120"
bool   own_m15 = own_tf == "15"
bool   own_m5  = own_tf == "5"
bool   own_on  = (own_h1 and use_h1) or (own_h2 and use_h2) or (own_m15 and use_m15) or (own_m5 and use_m5)
string own_nm  = own_h1 ? "H1" : own_h2 ? "H2" : own_m15 ? "M15" : "M5"
f_tf(own_on, true, own_m5, barstate.isconfirmed, own_tf, own_nm, d5_t,
     own_h1, own_h1 or own_m15, own_h1 or own_h2, own_m15 or own_m5, own_h1 or own_m15 or own_m5, false,
     d5_bpcl, d5_spcl, d5_ben, d5_sen, d5_benw, d5_senw, d5_boc, d5_soc, d5_bsb, d5_ssb,
     d5_c, d5_l, d5_h, d5_pl, d5_ph, d5_po, d5_lo2, d5_hi2, d5_boclv, d5_boctp, d5_soclv, d5_soctp, d5_blv, d5_btp, d5_slv, d5_stp,
     d5_bci, d5_sci, d5_bcilv, d5_bcitp, d5_scilv, d5_scitp, d5_cs)

var table note = table.new(position.top_right, 1, 1)
if show_nt and barstate.islast and not (own_h1 or own_h2 or own_m15 or own_m5)
    table.cell(note, 0, 0, "Entry Confirmations marks show on H1, H2, M15 or M5 charts. Alerts are sent from a 5-minute chart.",
         text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 40), text_size = size.small)
